## Differences and action plan

1. Enter does not submit the form (code, ❌). Add a keydown handler on the inner input: on Enter (not composing, not a modifier), call `this.form?.requestSubmit()` (after the native change), and add a Playwright test (type, press Enter, expect submit). Alternatively, if this is deemed out of scope, remove "and submits the form natively" from contract.json `accessibility.keyboard.Enter` and the md, and record a drift entry. Recommended: fix the code; users expect Enter to submit.
2. Defaults null vs '' (contract or code). Either change the contract to `""` for these string props (simplest, matches `.value` semantics) or reflect null. Also `label` and `description` reflect long text to attributes (mixin), which the contract does not declare; declare `reflect` or drop it.
3. Disabled dimming (code or contract). shadcn Field dims the whole field when disabled. Dim label and description too (a `:host([disabled])` rule using `--sb-input-disabled-opacity`) or state in the contract that only the control is dimmed.
4. Drift list incomplete (realization.web.drift). Add: focus ring solid `ring` rather than shadcn ring/50 (stated in json states.focus-visible note, absent from drift); Enter submit gap until fixed; mixin-provided `describedBy`/`renderDescription` are unused by Input (dead code, not a contract issue).
5. contract.md Realizations stale (contract): mark Web built, add coverage.

Verdict: needs code fix (Enter submit, item 1) and a small contract update (items 2-5).

Status (2026-11-15): open: item 2, contract.json does not declare that label, description and name reflect (a contract.json change needs a Figma re-sync of Input). Fixed in this PR: item 3, contract.md says only the control dims when disabled. Already fixed: item 1 (6dfe5c9, Enter submits the owning form), item 2 defaults (string props default to ""), items 4 and 5 (drift and Realizations updated).
